      <h2>Research Interests</h2>
      <p>
        My research lies at the intersection of epistemology, AI ethics, and
        philosophy of technology. I am especially interested in how trust,
        dependence, and responsibility are structured in human-AI relations.
        My current work develops a structural account of AI trust that asks
        whether human participants occupy fair and practically inhabitable roles
        within the relevant dependence relation.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also work on collective forgiveness, collective agency, and the
        practical-normative structure of interpersonal and political repair. More
        broadly, I am interested in virtue epistemology, skepticism,
        experimental philosophy, and the methodological status of philosophical
        intuitions.
      </p>

